<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/water-ceiling.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/water-ceiling-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/water-ceiling.webp 931w" sizes="100vw" width="931" height="621" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/">Services</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Water Damage Claim Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Water Damage Claim Appraisal in Virginia</h1><p class="lede">Water spreads farther than it looks. A supply-line leak or frozen pipe can run under floors and behind cabinets for days before anyone sees it, and the first estimate often stops at the visible stain.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Common causes</dt><dd>Frozen pipes, supply lines</dd></div><div><dt>Phases</dt><dd>Mitigation + rebuild</dd></div><div><dt>Watch for</dt><dd>Repeated-seepage exclusions</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Where water damage claim appraisal disputes come from</h2>
<p>Virginia winters are milder than New England’s, but cold snaps still freeze pipes in crawlspaces, exterior walls and seasonal homes in the mountains, especially in homes built for a mild climate. Add washing machine hoses, water heaters, ice-maker lines and roof leaks, and water losses are among the most common claims we see.</p>
<p>Disputes tend to center on:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mitigation invoices</strong> that the insurer cuts as excessive equipment or drying time.</li>
<li><strong>Scope of tear-out</strong>, such as how much drywall, insulation and flooring had to go.</li>
<li><strong>Matching</strong>: continuous flooring, cabinets and countertops that can’t be patched.</li>
<li><strong>Mold remediation</strong>, which policies often limit with a sub-limit.</li>
<li><strong>Cause and duration</strong>, because many policies exclude repeated seepage over 14 days or more.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How we value a water loss</h2>
<p>We review moisture logs, drying records and photos from the mitigation company, then inspect the rebuild scope ourselves. Our estimate prices each phase: demolition, drying, cleaning, rebuild and contents handling. That way the panel can see the full cost of putting the home back, not just the cost of drying it.</p>
<h3>Crawlspaces and basements</h3>
<p>Much of Hampton Roads and Southside builds on crawlspaces, while Northern Virginia and the mountains favor basements. Each hides damage differently. Wet subfloor, joists and insulation under a house are easy to leave out of an estimate.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Flood versus water damage</b>Water from a burst pipe is usually covered. Water from rising groundwater, surface runoff or tidal flooding usually isn’t covered under a homeowners policy. The source decides the policy.</div>
<h2>Questions about water damage claim appraisal</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>The insurer says the leak was long-term. What now?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Long-term seepage exclusions are common. Plumbing reports, moisture readings and the condition of the materials can help show when the water actually escaped.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is mold covered?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often only up to a sub-limit, and only when it results from a covered water loss. Check your policy’s fungi or mold endorsement.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="related"><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/fire-and-smoke-damage-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</span></a><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/tree-fall-and-ice-storm-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Fallen Tree &amp; Ice Storm Appraisal</span></a><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/historic-home-claim-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Historic Home Claim Appraisal</span></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><p class="box-small">Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET · All of Virginia</p></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">All services</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/commercial-and-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hail-and-roof-damage-app